00:09:57,305 --> 00:09:59,745
Because the two trucks were separated,

284
00:09:59,745 --> 00:10:02,506
Ford could make the F-one-fifty lighter and

285
00:10:02,506 --> 00:10:05,395
more comfortable, while making the Super Duty

286
00:10:05,395 --> 00:10:06,744
heavier and stronger.

287
00:10:06,924 --> 00:10:09,010
Each truck could be good at its

288
00:10:09,010 --> 00:10:11,434
own job, instead of one truck trying

289
00:10:11,434 --> 00:10:12,578
to do everything.

290
00:10:12,758 --> 00:10:15,753
Rivals eventually followed the same approach.

291
00:10:16,103 --> 00:10:17,865
In two thousand eleven,

292
00:10:17,865 --> 00:10:20,469
another quiet revolution happened.

293
00:10:20,649 --> 00:10:23,218
Ford put a twin-turbo V six,

294
00:10:23,218 --> 00:10:26,431
the EcoBoost, into the F-one-fifty.

295
00:10:26,611 --> 00:10:29,168
Many truck buyers swore they would never

296
00:10:29,168 --> 00:10:31,150
buy a pickup without a V eight.

297
00:10:31,330 --> 00:10:32,479
Then they drove it.

298
00:10:32,659 --> 00:10:35,134
The EcoBoost became one of the most

299
00:10:35,134 --> 00:10:37,255
popular engines in the lineup,

300
00:10:37,255 --> 00:10:40,295
and it changed what Americans expected from

301
00:10:40,295 --> 00:10:41,355
a truck engine.

302
00:10:41,705 --> 00:10:43,342
Turning point number four.

303
00:10:43,522 --> 00:10:44,683
Twenty fifteen.

304
00:10:44,863 --> 00:10:47,990
Ford did something no other mass-market truck

305
00:10:47,990 --> 00:10:49,519
maker had dared to do.

306
00:10:49,699 --> 00:10:52,043
It built the body of the F-one-fifty

307
00:10:52,043 --> 00:10:54,192
out of aluminum instead of steel.

308
00:10:54,372 --> 00:10:56,664
The truck lost a lot of weight,

309
00:10:56,664 --> 00:10:58,587
which helped fuel economy,

310
00:10:58,587 --> 00:10:59,991
towing and payload.

311
00:11:00,171 --> 00:11:01,518
Competitors mocked it.

312
00:11:01,698 --> 00:11:04,387
Some ads even questioned whether aluminum was

313
00:11:04,387 --> 00:11:06,180
tough enough for a real truck.

314
00:11:06,529 --> 00:11:08,166
Ford's argument was simple.

315
00:11:08,346 --> 00:11:11,456
Aluminum is the material used in airplanes

316
00:11:11,456 --> 00:11:13,455
and many military vehicles.

317
00:11:13,635 --> 00:11:15,353
It does not rust like steel.

318
00:11:15,533 --> 00:11:17,677
And a lighter truck can carry and

319
00:11:17,677 --> 00:11:19,562
tow more for the same engine.

320
00:11:19,742 --> 00:11:22,617
Critics argued that repairs would cost more

321
00:11:22,617 --> 00:11:25,024
and that insurers would charge more.

322
00:11:25,204 --> 00:11:26,176
For a while,

323
00:11:26,176 --> 00:11:28,037
both sides had a point.

324
00:11:28,387 --> 00:11:30,175
The switch was enormous.

325
00:11:30,355 --> 00:11:33,103
Ford had to retool its factories,

326
00:11:33,103 --> 00:11:34,518
train body shops,

327
00:11:34,518 --> 00:11:36,683
and convince loyal buyers.

328
00:11:36,863 --> 00:11:37,911
For a while,

329
00:11:37,911 --> 00:11:41,054
sales slowed as plants changed over.

330
00:11:41,234 --> 00:11:42,674
But the bet paid off.

331
00:11:42,854 --> 00:11:46,118
The aluminum F-one-fifty kept the sales crown,

332
00:11:46,118 --> 00:11:48,602
and the material became part of the

333
00:11:48,602 --> 00:11:49,808
truck's identity.

334
00:11:50,158 --> 00:11:51,603
Now here is the twist,

335
00:11:51,603 --> 00:11:53,572
and it is happening right now.

336
00:11:53,752 --> 00:11:57,036
Using aluminum made the F-Series depend on

337
00:11:57,036 --> 00:11:59,928
a small number of aluminum suppliers.

338
00:12:00,108 --> 00:12:01,950
On September sixteenth,

339
00:12:01,950 --> 00:12:05,074
twenty twenty-five, a fire broke out at

340
00:12:05,074 --> 00:12:08,037
the Novelis aluminum plant in Oswego,

341
00:12:08,037 --> 00:12:08,758
New York.

342
00:12:08,938 --> 00:12:10,517
On November twentieth,

343
00:12:10,517 --> 00:12:13,244
a second significant fire hit the same

344
00:12:13,244 --> 00:12:13,675
plant.

345
00:12:13,855 --> 00:12:16,627
That plant supplies a large share of

346
00:12:16,627 --> 00:12:19,323
the aluminum sheet for Ford trucks.

347
00:12:19,672 --> 00:12:21,286
The damage was real.

348
00:12:21,466 --> 00:12:24,054
According to Automotive Logistics,

349
00:12:24,054 --> 00:12:28,088
Ford's chief financial officer Sherry House confirmed

350
00:12:28,088 --> 00:12:30,981
a production loss of about one hundred

351
00:12:30,981 --> 00:12:34,330
thousand vehicles across twenty twenty-five.

352
00:12:34,510 --> 00:12:37,959
On the February twenty twenty-six earnings call,

353
00:12:37,959 --> 00:12:40,833
chief executive Jim Farley referred to a

354
00:12:40,833 --> 00:12:43,994
two billion dollar headwind from the Novelis

355
00:12:43,994 --> 00:12:44,425
fires.

356
00:12:44,605 --> 00:12:47,160
Novelis said it expected to restart the

357
00:12:47,160 --> 00:12:49,452
hot mill late in the second quarter

358
00:12:49,452 --> 00:12:50,828
of twenty twenty-six.

359
00:12:51,177 --> 00:12:53,930
For buyers, the effect was visible on

360
00:12:53,930 --> 00:12:54,823
dealer lots.

361
00:12:55,003 --> 00:12:58,826
Ford Authority reported in October twenty twenty-five

362
00:12:58,826 --> 00:13:02,576
that F-one-fifty production at the Dearborn assembly

363
00:13:02,576 --> 00:13:05,678
plant was cut sharply while aluminum supply

364
00:13:05,678 --> 00:13:06,543
was limited.

365
00:13:06,723 --> 00:13:10,021
Fewer trucks being built usually means fewer

366
00:13:10,021 --> 00:13:13,244
discounts, and buyers who wanted a specific

367
00:13:13,244 --> 00:13:16,391
configuration sometimes had to wait or pay

368
00:13:16,391 --> 00:13:16,766
more.

369
00:13:17,115 --> 00:13:20,194
So the decision that helped the F-one-fifty

370
00:13:20,194 --> 00:13:22,843
win in twenty fifteen became its weak

371
00:13:22,843 --> 00:13:24,418
point ten years later.

372
00:13:24,598 --> 00:13:26,985
One supplier, one city,

373
00:13:26,985 --> 00:13:27,919
one fire.

374
00:13:28,099 --> 00:13:30,394
Ford said it planned to add fifty

375
00:13:30,394 --> 00:13:33,176
to sixty thousand units of production in

376
00:13:33,176 --> 00:13:35,680
twenty twenty-six to make up for the

377
00:13:35,680 --> 00:13:36,028
loss.

378
00:13:36,208 --> 00:13:38,138
It shows how a single part of

379
00:13:38,138 --> 00:13:40,865
a supply chain can shake the best-selling

380
00:13:40,865 --> 00:13:42,129
vehicle in America.

381
00:13:42,479 --> 00:13:44,140
Turning point number five.

382
00:13:44,320 --> 00:13:45,683
The electric bet,

383
00:13:45,683 --> 00:13:46,885
and the U-turn.

384
00:13:47,065 --> 00:13:48,619
In twenty twenty-one,

385
00:13:48,619 --> 00:13:52,467
Ford launched the fourteenth-generation F-one-fifty,

386
00:13:52,467 --> 00:13:55,204
including a hybrid called PowerBoost.

387
00:13:55,384 --> 00:13:56,963
Then came the big one.

388
00:13:57,143 --> 00:13:59,026
The F-one-fifty Lightning,

389
00:13:59,026 --> 00:14:00,765
a fully electric pickup,

390
00:14:00,765 --> 00:14:03,227
using the name of the nineties hot

391
00:14:03,227 --> 00:14:03,517
rod.

392
00:14:03,697 --> 00:14:04,706
Orders poured in,

393
00:14:04,706 --> 00:14:06,488
and for a while it looked like

394
00:14:06,488 --> 00:14:07,853
the future had arrived.

395
00:14:08,203 --> 00:14:09,597
It did not last.

396
00:14:09,777 --> 00:14:11,739
According to Fox Business,

397
00:14:11,739 --> 00:14:13,399
on December sixteenth,

398
00:14:13,399 --> 00:14:17,248
twenty twenty-five, Ford announced a nineteen point

399
00:14:17,248 --> 00:14:20,266
five billion dollar charge as it changed

400
00:14:20,266 --> 00:14:22,530
its electric vehicle strategy,

401
00:14:22,530 --> 00:14:26,379
and ended production of the all-electric Lightning.

402
00:14:26,559 --> 00:14:29,586
In the third quarter of twenty twenty-six,

403
00:14:29,586 --> 00:14:31,531
according to autoevolution,

404
00:14:31,531 --> 00:14:35,135
Ford sold just two hundred eighty-nine Lightnings,

405
00:14:35,135 --> 00:14:37,801
compared with ten thousand and five a

406
00:14:37,801 --> 00:14:38,738
year earlier.

407
00:14:39,087 --> 00:14:39,993
What went wrong?

408
00:14:40,173 --> 00:14:41,845
Price was a big part of it.

409
00:14:42,025 --> 00:14:44,502
Electric trucks cost more to build,

410
00:14:44,502 --> 00:14:46,980
and when the federal tax credit for

411
00:14:46,980 --> 00:14:50,236
electric vehicles ended in twenty twenty-five,

412
00:14:50,236 --> 00:14:51,510
the gap got wider.

413
00:14:51,690 --> 00:14:53,327
Towing range was another.

414
00:14:53,507 --> 00:14:55,848
A heavy trailer could cut the range

415
00:14:55,848 --> 00:14:58,189
of an electric pickup dramatically,

416
00:14:58,189 --> 00:14:59,928
and many truck buyers tow.

417
00:15:00,108 --> 00:15:02,218
The Lightning was a great truck for

418
00:15:02,218 --> 00:15:04,450
